  "Question": "Ahn chooses a two-digit integer, subtracts it from \\(200,\\) and doubles the result. What is the largest number Ahn can get?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(200\\)",
    "B": "\\(202\\)",
    "C": "\\(220\\)",
    "D": "\\(380\\)",
    "E": "\\(398\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Subtracting a smaller number from \\(200\\) leaves a larger result, and doubling preserves that order. Thus Ahn should choose the smallest two-digit number, \\(10\\). The largest result is\n\\[\n2(200-10)=2\\cdot190=\\boxed{380},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
